ry counts are performed at all warehouse locations. Count teams include personnel independent of the warehouse function. Discrepancies exceeding 2% of book value trigger a recount. Last quarter, two of five locations did not complete recounts for flagged items within the required timeframe.', freq_quarterly: 'Quarterly', c4_account: 'Foreign Currency Translation', c4_process: 'Financial Close', c4_desc: 'The treasury department uses month-end spot rates from Bloomberg terminal to translate foreign subsidiary balances. Translation adjustments are reviewed by the assistant controller and posted to other comprehensive income. Rate sources are documented in the close package.', c5_account: 'Property, Plant and Equipment', c5_process: 'Capital Expenditure', c5_desc: 'Capital expenditure requests above $50,000 require dual approval (department head and CFO). The fixed asset register is reconciled to the GL monthly. However, the authorization threshold has not been updated since 2018 and inflation has reduced its effective gatekeeping function. Items between $25,000 and $50,000 are approved by department heads alone.', c6_account: 'Income Tax Provision', c6_process: 'Tax Compliance', c6_desc: 'External tax advisors compute the quarterly income tax provision using a detailed model. The tax director reviews assumptions and rates. Year-end true-up is reconciled to filed returns. The process is well-documented with a tax provision binder maintained for each period.', c7_account: 'IT General Controls', c7_process: 'Access Management', c7_desc: 'User access reviews are performed semi-annually by application owners. Terminated employee accounts should be disabled within 24 hours per policy. However, a recent review found 12 active accounts belonging to employees who left the company more than 30 days prior. Root cause analysis was not performed.', freq_semi_annual: 'Semi-Annual', c8_account: 'Accounts Receivable', c8_process: 'Order-to-Cash', c8_desc: 'The allowance for doubtful accounts is estimated quarterly using an aging analysis. The credit manager reviews accounts over 90 days past due individually. Write-off authority is limited to the controller for amounts above $5,000. Methodology and assumptions are documented in the close checklist.', c9_account: 'Financial Statement Disclosures', c9_process: 'Financial Reporting', c9_desc: 'A disclosure checklist aligned with ASC 235 and SEC Regulation S-X is completed each quarter. The checklist is reviewed by the controller and external auditors provide commentary. Two disclosure items related to segment reporting were flagged as incomplete in the prior quarter but were corrected before filing.', c10_account: 'Journal Entries', c10_process: 'Financial Close', c10_desc: 'Non-standard journal entries above $25,000 require approval by the controller or CFO before posting. The system enforces segregation of duties — the preparer cannot be the approver. Monthly, a report of all manual journal entries is generated and reviewed for unusual items. The review is documented with sign-off.', auto_yes: 'Yes', auto_no: 'No', chart_compliance: 'Compliance Score (%)', chart_doc_quality: 'Documentation Quality (%)', chart_trends_title: 'Compliance and Documentation Trends', chart_cum_deficiencies: 'Cumulative Deficiencies', chart_deficiency_title: 'Deficiency Tracking', perf_needs_improvement: 'Needs Improvement', perf_excellent: 'Excellent — Audit-Ready', perf_proficient: 'Proficient', perf_developing: 'Developing', ins_assertions: 'Review how controls map to the five financial statement assertions (existence, completeness, valuation, rights, presentation).', ins_classification: 'Strengthen your understanding of what distinguishes a key control from a non-key control under PCAOB AS 2201.', ins_effectiveness: 'Focus on evaluating design effectiveness by looking for gaps between policy and actual practice.', ins_samples: 'PCAOB standards require adequate sample sizes. Key controls with higher risk need larger